WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.350
Vietnam, the 1950s and 60s.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.710
War spreads through the countryside.

3
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.300
Villages near the monasteries are bombed.

4
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:10.740
Stay in the monastery and keep practising?

5
00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:13.240
Or go out to the bombed villages?

6
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:17.310
Some monks and nuns gave an answer
that would shape a whole movement.

7
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.020
So, if bombs are falling near your temple,

8
00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.940
do you keep meditating or go out to help?

9
00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:26.150
In this mission, you'll see
what Engaged Buddhism means,

10
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.170
and the teachings that drive it.

11
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.990
Then you'll read 2 verses
from the Dhammapada,

12
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.560
one on killing and one on hatred.

13
00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:37.920
Your mission: find out whether a Buddhist
should keep meditating or go out to

14
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.390
help, and why.
